{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "EDGARv81MonthlyEmis",
    "description": "EDGAR v8.1 monthly global air pollutant emissions data loader. Provides surface-layer volumetric emission rate (kg m⁻³ s⁻¹) for lev < 2 (first vertical layer), and zero above. Configured per substance (species) and emission sector at instantiation time via {species} and {sector} URL template substitutions.\n\nSupported substances: BC, CO, NH3, NMVOC, NOx, OC, PM10, PM2.5, SO2.\nData spans 2000–2022 at 0.1°×0.1° global resolution, with monthly temporal resolution.\n\nThe gt-p3ep (@register_symbolic interp_unsafe) blocking gap is resolved by the data_loaders §8 mechanism: the runtime handles file download, temporal interpolation, and spatial regridding to the model domain; the model equation references the loader variable directly via EDGAR_v81.flx. No registered functions remain in the migrated component.\n\nEquation: emission = ifelse(lev < 2, EDGAR_v81.flx / Δz * scale, 0)\nwhere EDGAR_v81.flx is the emission flux (kg m⁻² s⁻¹) regridded by the runtime from the 0.1°×0.1° EDGAR grid to the model domain, and Δz (default 60 m) is the first-layer height that converts the surface flux to a volumetric rate.\n\nMigrated from EarthSciData.jl@830435a src/edgar_v81_monthly.jl:277 (EDGARv81MonthlyEmis, esm-yp9q).\n\n[esm-3nc.3] Split into a pure-I/O loader (edgar_v81_monthly_loader.esm) + this regridding model per RFC pure-io-data-loaders §6/§7. The loader is referenced as the subsystem EDGAR_v81; the surface flux is regridded conservatively (cell-centered emissions).",
    "tags": [
      "earthsci_data",
      "emissions",
      "anthropogenic",
      "edgar",
      "monthly",
      "data_loader",
      "surface_flux",
      "regridding_model"
    ],
    "created": "2026-05-30T00:00:00Z",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciData.jl contributors",
      "EarthSciModels migration (esm-yp9q)"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Crippa, M., Guizzardi, D., Butler, T., Keating, T., Wu, R., Rosenveld, M., Jonescu, M., Muntean, M., Schaaf, E., Oreggioni, G., Gonzalez Ortiz, A., Textor, R., Sarigiannis, D., Muntean, M. (2023). EDGAR v8.1 Global Air Pollutant Emissions (1970–2022). European Commission, Joint Research Centre (JRC). Available: https://edgar.jrc.ec.europa.eu/dataset_ap81",
        "url": "https://edgar.jrc.ec.europa.eu/dataset_ap81"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Source: EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/edgar_v81_monthly.jl:91-338 (EDGARv81MonthlyEmisFileSet, EDGARv81MonthlyEmis constructor). Test: test/edgar_v81_monthly_test.jl."
      }
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
    "EDGAR_v81": {
      "kind": "grid",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "https://jeodpp.jrc.ec.europa.eu/ftp/jrc-opendata/EDGAR/datasets/v81_FT2022_AP_new/monthly/{species}/bkl_{sector}/bkl_{sector}_flx_nc.zip"
      },
      "temporal": {
        "start": "2000-01-01T00:00:00Z",
        "end": "2022-12-31T23:59:59Z",
        "file_period": "P1Y",
        "frequency": "P1M",
        "records_per_file": 12,
        "time_variable": "time"
      },
      "reference": {
        "citation": "Crippa, M. et al. (2023). EDGAR v8.1 Global Air Pollutant Emissions (1970–2022). European Commission, Joint Research Centre (JRC). Available: https://edgar.jrc.ec.europa.eu/dataset_ap81",
        "url": "https://edgar.jrc.ec.europa.eu/dataset_ap81"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "emissions",
          "anthropogenic",
          "edgar",
          "monthly",
          "gridded"
        ],
        "earthscidata_source": "src/edgar_v81_monthly.jl::EDGARv81MonthlyEmisFileSet",
        "valid_species": [
          "BC",
          "CO",
          "NH3",
          "NMVOC",
          "NOx",
          "OC",
          "PM10",
          "PM2.5",
          "SO2"
        ],
        "packaging": "zip-of-netcdf",
        "unit_note": "Raw NC file may declare units 'kg m-2 s-1'; the loadmetadata function reads var.attrib['units'] and applies to_unit() conversion — default assumed if attribute absent.",
        "native_resolution_deg": {
          "lon": 0.1,
          "lat": 0.1
        },
        "native_extent": {
          "lon": [
            -180.0,
            180.0
          ],
          "lat": [
            -90.0,
            90.0
          ]
        },
        "proj4_string": "+proj=longlat +datum=WGS84 +no_defs",
        "former_regridding": "Pre-migration per-loader regridding block was {fill_value: 0.0, extrapolation: clamp}; at 0.7.0 regridding became a per-variable model `regrid` map; 0.8.0 removed that too \u2014 the kernel is now a coupling expression (esm-spec \u00a78.6), and edgar_v81_monthly.esm keeps the per-variable choice verbatim in Model.reference.notes.",
        "native_grid_family": "cartesian",
        "native_crs_epsg": "EPSG:4326 (geographic longlat / WGS84). At esm 0.8.0 the crs is documentation only — a data source no longer carries a `grid`/crs descriptor; the longlat identity reprojection is applied at the coupling edge via ESD reprojection/longlat.esm (esd-47z.1).",
        "native_crs_descriptor": {
          "projection": "longlat",
          "datum": "WGS84"
        },
        "native_dimensions": [
          "lon",
          "lat"
        ],
        "native_dimension_extents": {
          "lon": {
            "n": 3600,
            "spacing": "uniform"
          },
          "lat": {
            "n": 1800,
            "spacing": "uniform"
          }
        },
        "native_staggering": "Cell-centered (lon 'center', lat 'center') — the native EDGAR v8.1 0.1°×0.1° lattice is a regular non-staggered raster (the former `grid.description`, preserved verbatim in native_grid_description, said 'cell-centered'). At esm 0.8.0 the regridding kernel is a coupling expression, not a model `regrid` block; the per-variable kernel choice is recorded verbatim in edgar_v81_monthly.esm's Model.reference.notes.",
        "native_grid_description": "Native EDGAR v8.1 grid: regular global 0.1°×0.1° longitude/latitude lattice, cell-centered. Geographic (unprojected) crs — the regridding model applies the longlat identity reprojection (ESD reprojection/longlat.esm, esd-47z.1). Migrated from the loader's former DataLoaderSpatial block (proj4 +proj=longlat +datum=WGS84); the loader describes this grid but performs no reprojection or regridding. Documented native geometry: lon ∈ [-180°, 180°] (3600 cells), lat ∈ [-90°, 90°] (1800 cells).",
        "migration_note": "esm 0.7.0 -> 0.8.0: removed the `grid` block (family/crs/dimensions/extents/description), which no schema at or after 0.8.0 permits — 0.8.0 deleted the native-grid descriptor outright (esm-spec §8.4; the 1.0.0 DataSource is additionalProperties:false over {kind, source, temporal, determinism, reader_options, select, record_filter, extent, reference, metadata}, with no `grid` key). Nothing was dropped: `family` → native_grid_family; `crs` → native_crs_epsg + native_crs_descriptor (verbatim); `dimensions` → native_dimensions; `extents` (per-dimension cell count + spacing) → native_dimension_extents; `description` → native_grid_description (verbatim). Native grid geometry is now ordinary data — a source exposes its coordinates/connectivity/metric arrays as ordinary `file_variable`s bound to consuming parameters, and reprojection/regridding are ordinary `aggregate` coupling expressions (esm-spec §8.6), not a loader `grid` or a model `regrid` block. No other field changed."
      }
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "EDGARv81MonthlyEmis": {
      "reference": {
        "notes": "source_ref: EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/edgar_v81_monthly.jl:277\n\nUpstream constructor EDGARv81MonthlyEmis(substance, sector, domaininfo; scale=1.0, ...) creates an MTK System with:\n  - @parameters: lon (rad), lat (rad), lev (1), Δz=60.0 (m), t_ref=get_tref(domaininfo) (s)\n  - One DataSetInterpolator per varnames(fileset): builds interp_unsafe equation for each NC variable\n  - Equation template (from create_interp_equation with wrapper_f):\n      var(t) ~ ifelse(lev < 2, interp_unsafe(data, fit, fi_lon, fi_lat, extrap) * unit_scale / Δz * scale, zero_var)\n    where fit = 1 + (t_ref + t - tstart) / tstep\n          fi_lon = 1 + (lon - s1start) / s1step\n          fi_lat = 1 + (lat - s2start) / s2step\n  - discrete_events: build_interp_event fires at monthly tstops to reload data buffers\n  - metadata: Dict(CoupleType => EDGARv81MonthlyEmisCoupler, SysDomainInfo => domaininfo)\n\ngt-p3ep resolution: the @register_symbolic interp_unsafe pattern is replaced by the data_loaders §8\nmechanism. EDGAR_v81.flx is the loader variable that the runtime regridds from the 0.1°×0.1° EDGAR\ngrid to the model domain and interpolates in time to t. The runtime implicitly handles the\nbuild_interp_event discrete callbacks based on data_loaders.temporal.frequency = P1M.\n\nParameter rename: upstream `t` (simulation time relative to t_ref) is implicit; the ESM model\nhas no independent variable in the variable map since it only contains observed equations.\n\nThe variable `emission` corresponds to the observed variable created by the for-loop over\nvarnames(fileset). For the typical single-variable EDGAR NC file (one flux variable per\nsubstance/sector), there is one observed equation. The variable name in the NC file is 'flx'\n(from the _flx_nc.zip filename convention; confirmed by ESS test fixture at\nEarthSciAST/pkg/earthsci-ast-py/tests/fixtures/data_loaders/edgar_v81_monthly.esm).\n\n--- esm-3nc.3 pure-IO split ---\nThis is the regridding-model half of the pure-IO loader migration (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §6/§7, bead esm-3nc.3). The pre-migration edgar_v81_monthly.esm carried both this coupler model AND a co-located data_loaders.EDGAR_v81 block (with the now-removed `spatial` and `regridding` sub-blocks). That loader is now the pure-I/O file components/earthsci_data/edgar_v81_monthly_loader.esm, referenced here as the subsystem `EDGAR_v81`; the observed `emission` expression references the regridded loader field directly as EDGAR_v81.flx.\nReprojection (RFC §6 step 2): EDGAR's native grid.crs.projection is 'longlat' (geographic WGS84), so the reprojection rule selected by convention is ESD reprojection/longlat.esm (esd-47z.1) — the IDENTITY transform.\nRegridding (RFC §6 step 3 / §5.2): the EDGAR flux is a cell-centered scalar → conservative area-weighted overlap join (ESD regridding/conservative_regrid_overlap_join.esm), declared in the model `regrid` block.\n\nCoupler identity: this model was serialized with the model-level field `coupletype: \"EDGARv81MonthlyEmisCoupler\"`, the EarthSciMLBase `CoupleType` metadata tag naming the Julia coupler struct that `EarthSciMLBase.couple2` dispatches on to find this component's pairwise coupling rules. The esm schema defined `coupletype` only before 0.8.0 (\"informational label identifying this system's role in coupling\"); 0.8.0 removed it in favour of explicit coupling — `coupling` entries naming components directly, or `coupling_roles` + `coupling_import` in a coupling-library file (esm-spec §10.9–§10.11). esm 1.0.0 has no model-level coupler-identity field, so the tag is recorded here to keep it recoverable.\n\nRegridding intent: this model was serialized with the model-level `regrid` map, one entry per variable naming the kernel that carries the loaded native-grid field onto the consuming model's grid. The esm schema defined `regrid` only before 0.8.0. esm 1.0.0 states (esm-spec §8.6) that a data source performs no regridding and that there is NO `Model.regrid` map: the carrier is the `variable_map` entry's `transform` field on the coupling edge that consumes the field (§10.4/§10.5) — an ordinary `aggregate` expression, typically an `apply_expression_template` invocation of an imported overlap-weight library. No such coupling edge exists in this document, so the map is recorded here VERBATIM to keep every field recoverable. This is a demotion from a structured field to prose, not an equivalent: the transform expression still has to be authored on whichever coupling edge consumes these fields.\n\n`regrid` (verbatim):\n{\n  \"flx\": {\n    \"method\": \"conservative\",\n    \"description\": \"EDGAR surface emission flux (kg m⁻² s⁻¹). Cell-centered emissions scalar → conservative area-weighted overlap-join regridder (ESD regridding/conservative_regrid_overlap_join.esm). Referenced by the `emission` observed as EDGAR_v81.flx.\"\n  }\n}"
      },
      "tolerance": {
        "rel": 1e-06
      },
      "variables": {
        "lon": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "rad",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Longitude of the grid point (radians). Coupled to the simulation domain's longitude coordinate via param_to_var when composed into a CoupledSystem."
        },
        "lat": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "rad",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Latitude of the grid point (radians). Coupled to the simulation domain's latitude coordinate via param_to_var when composed into a CoupledSystem."
        },
        "lev": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "Vertical level index (dimensionless, 1-based). Emissions are applied only at lev < 2 (surface layer). Coupled to the simulation domain's lev coordinate via param_to_var when composed into a CoupledSystem."
        },
        "Δz": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 60.0,
          "description": "Height of the first vertical grid layer (m). Used to convert surface emission flux (kg m⁻² s⁻¹) to volumetric emission rate (kg m⁻³ s⁻¹) via division."
        },
        "scale": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "Multiplicative scaling factor applied to the emission flux. Default 1.0 (no scaling). May be used to adjust emissions for sensitivity experiments or unit-system conversions."
        },
        "emission": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/m^3/s",
          "description": "Volumetric emission rate (kg m⁻³ s⁻¹) at the current grid point and time. Non-zero only in the surface layer (lev < 2): emission = EDGAR_v81.flx / Δz * scale. Zero for lev ≥ 2. Corresponds to the upstream observed variable created per varnames(fileset) by create_interp_equation with wrapper_f = eq -> ifelse(lev < 2, eq / Δz * scale, zero_emis)."
        },
        "flx": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "kg/m^2/s",
          "shape": [],
          "description": "Surface emission flux for the configured species and sector. Variable name 'flx' is derived from the _flx_nc.zip archive naming convention for EDGAR v8.1 AP datasets.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "EDGAR_v81",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "flx",
              "description": "Surface emission flux for the configured species and sector. Variable name 'flx' is derived from the _flx_nc.zip archive naming convention for EDGAR v8.1 AP datasets."
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": "emission",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "ifelse",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "<",
                "args": [
                  "lev",
                  2.0
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "/",
                    "args": [
                      "flx",
                      "Δz"
                    ]
                  },
                  "scale"
                ]
              },
              0.0
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "tests": []
    }
  }
}
